<title>USA: Lingering showers in Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</title>
<headline>Lingering showers in Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Intensifying low pressure building along the coast of Buenos Aires this weekend will be unable to bring any cold air into Brazil's coffee belt, Weather Services Corp said in an update on Friday.</p>
<p>According to WSC, the system is expected to weaken and head out to sea during the early part of next week.</p>
<p>Clearing skies across the region this morning kept temperatures near normal. Lows this morning ranged from 50-59 F (10-15 C).</p>
<p>The outlook calls for fair to partly cloudy skies today with a few lingering showers for the region. Partly to variably cloudy skies are expected through the weekend. Temperatures should remain near normal levels with lows in the 50's to low 60's F (low to middle teens C).</p>
<p>&quot;There are no threats of cold weather for the coffee belt on today's extended range maps,&quot; WSC said.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212 859-1640))</p>
</text>
